# SSH allowed-signers for release tag verification.
#
# The release workflow runs:
#
#     git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile .github/allowed-signers
#     git -c gpg.format=ssh verify-tag "$TAG"
#
# and refuses to publish if the tag is not signed by a key listed here. The
# workflow fails closed when this file is absent or empty, so the first release
# after this change will stop with a clear error rather than publishing
# unverified.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT — one line per key, multiple keys per maintainer supported
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#
jp@theqrl.org      namespaces="git"	ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDDxjmwacZTwYiRCOozapgXHMlx8EkdFXPvXu0s02ZPz
